  "description": "Human approval over HTTP for Invarix.Gate. In enforce mode, when a policy escalates a tool call, the broker posts an approval request to a webhook and waits; an operator opens the confirmation page, reads what the agent is trying to do, and approves, denies, or stops the run. A GET only renders, so mail scanners and chat link previewers that prefetch the link cannot decide anything. Approval tokens carry 256 bits of entropy, are stored only as a SHA-256 hash, and are consumed once. The request payload and the page show the findings and a capped preview of the tool arguments with credentials masked by pattern: every credential shape Gate's secret-egress detector recognises by pattern, including Azure storage keys and passwords inside database URIs, and the password in a scheme://user:password@ URI of any scheme. A credential with no recognisable shape, or a value flagged only by the detector's opt-in high-entropy fallback, can appear as sent. Delivery to a broken webhook fails in seconds rather than absorbing the approval timeout. Needs a Gate license token, free below the Community revenue threshold and paid above it. Terms: https://invarix.dk/gate.",
